# Development Guidelines

## Testing and Documentation
- Always update tests and documentation when making feature changes or modifying behavior
- Tests should cover new functionality, edge cases, and validation logic
- Documentation should reflect user-facing changes, new features, and updated output formats
- When adding new methods or changing existing behavior, ensure both tests and docs are updated

## Code Quality
- Follow existing code style and patterns
- Add appropriate error handling and validation
- Include helpful comments for complex logic
- Maintain consistency with existing codebase structure
